      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "NEIL THE SEAL (3) flew the lids off the inside draw with a fast early split and gave a sight, finishing a 2.5 lengths second (30.42) over 525m at this track. One of the leading chances. WAH CEDAR (7) was strongly fancied latest and proved too good with a one length win at this track in a handy 30.44. Draws out wide but goes well over this trip. Comes out of a solid form race last start. Expected to feature again. WEBLEC RACHAEL (4) has been settling off the speed lately, finishing sixth (23.35) last time in a Restricted WIN H at Geelong. Has the ability to give this a shake. GODZILLA (1) has not raced here but still warrants respect.",
